#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Director-adjudicated theorem and source ledgers; no inference from source access."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
A='audits/adversarial_reviews/'
def read(p):
 f=R/p
 return [json.loads(x) for x in f.read_text().splitlines() if x.strip()] if f.exists() else []
def write(p,rows):(R/p).write_text(''.join(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n' for x in rows))
def upsert(p,rows):
 d={x['id']:x for x in read(p)};d.update({x['id']:x for x in rows});write(p,list(d.values()))
N={k:A+'director_'+v+'_round11.md' for k,v in [('joint','joint_brownian'),('matrix','integer_trace'),('global','global_hardy'),('deninger','deninger_whole'),('drift','suzuki_drift'),('bands','polynomial_bands')]}
C=[]
def c(i,k,s,h,kind,paper=None):
 C.append(dict(id=i,paper_id=paper,statement=s,hypotheses=h,claim_kind=kind,locator=N[k],status='adjudicated_scoped',novelty_claim=False))
c('THM-HLZ-JOURNAL5-REAL-COEFFICIENTS','bands','For real Dirichlet Q(s)=sum_(n<=T^delta) a(n)n^(−s), delta<1/2, the shifted zero sum in HLZ Theorem 5 equals J(alpha,beta,T)+I(alpha,beta,T)+I(beta,alpha,T)+O_A(T(log T)^(−A)) for every fixed A>0. J and I are the exact expressions in journal equations (5) and (24).','Unconditional published input; |alpha|,|beta|<=c/log T, fixed small c; common fixed divisor-log coefficient envelope and |a(mn)| bounded by a constant times |a(m)a(n)|; the bounded unit coefficient is treated separately. The real-coefficient specialization avoids hidden conjugation conventions. Theorem 5 is distinct from the smoothing Lemma 6/Theorem 4. Sharp continuous input is independently reconstructed.','matched_published_primary_theorem','PAPER-DM63-HLZ2022')
c('THM-JOINT-PRIME-GAUSSIAN-ARRAY','joint','Under RH, fixed-dimensional cosine/sine normalized prime arrays on p ≤ (log Y)^D with covariance Σ_Y → Σ finite tend to N(0, Σ) if and only if max_p(‖a_p‖ + ‖b_p‖) → 0. Sufficiency is effective with computable fixed parameters and convergence moduli.','Exact symmetric strict tail probability weighted by |ζ′|²/(1/4 + γ²). The covariance uses v_p = (1 − 1/p)/2. The real coordinate is centered by p^(−1/2) and the imaginary coordinate by 0. Necessity uses unrestricted qualitative comparison and Cramér’s theorem. Singular covariance is allowed. Orthant effectivity requires positive limiting marginal variances.','conditional_joint_array_gaussian_criterion')
c('THM-FINITE-VARIANCE-PRIME-ANNULI','joint','Under RH, disjoint centered unnormalized cosine bands (log Y)^(a_i) < p ≤ (log Y)^(b_i) have independent Gaussian limits of variance (1/2) log(b_i/a_i), for fixed positive separated exponent intervals.','Columns tend to zero as their primes tend to infinity. The variance need not diverge. Standardized cumulative cutoffs at (log Y)^D have limiting correlation 1.','conditional_moving_band_limit')
c('THM-PRIME-BROWNIAN-PROCESS','joint','Under RH, set L = log Y, b = log L, H = log b, and X_Y(u) = √(2/H) Σ_{p ≤ exp(b^u)} [cos(γ log p)/√p − 1/p]. For fixed 0 ≤ u₀ < 1, X_Y converges to standard Brownian motion restricted to [u₀, 1] in D with the J₁ topology. An effective conditional bounded-Lipschitz onset exists for computable parameters.','The same exact two-sign strict derivative-weighted law applies. The proof uses uniform subset fourth moments bounded by C(Σ 1/p)², exact reciprocal-clock interpolation, an all-time modulus, and finite-dimensional comparison. Numerical onset and the unweighted zero law are outside this result.','conditional_functional_limit')
c('THM-INTEGER-TOEPLITZ-PURITY','matrix','A monic integral q-reciprocal polynomial of degree d with nonzero roots and integer q ≥ 1 is pure of radius √q if and only if K_{ij} = q^min(i,j) t_{|i−j|} is positive semidefinite for 0 ≤ i,j < d, where t_n = Σ α^n and t₀ = d. Its inertia is (c + b, b, d − c − 2b), with c distinct circle roots and b off-circle reciprocal-conjugate pairs.','Multiplicities are positive, and real coefficients give conjugate closure. Repeated roots and reducibility are allowed. Exact Newton traces through d − 1 and rational pivoting give a polynomial-bit algorithm. The classical power-sum Toeplitz criterion is credited to Heinig–Rost.','classical_criterion_arithmetic_specialization')
c('CERT-GLOBAL-HARDY-C2','global','Unconditionally, the distinct-critical-line derivative series satisfies 0.61649875288731141829 < C₂ < 1.075561. The tail beyond 10,000 is less than 0.45906151 by global variation of Q₂Z/t with rational parameters and a complete infinite residual bound.','Uses the existing full 160-bit census of 10,142 positive zeros, independent replays, and the director’s 192-bit bound. RH is used only to identify the tapered-array limit. The quartic splice near 0.65339 remains observational.','validated_unconditional_full_series_interval')
c('THM-DENINGER-REAL-DESCENT-OBSTRUCTION','deninger','A real equivariant central spectral space satisfying Artin multiplicity axiom 2.12 is impossible at a Galois field with a quaternionic irreducible representation of odd central Artin order. Such Q₈ fields exist, excluding a universal arithmetic-curve theory with these properties.','The audit pins the complete arXiv:2204.02714v2 and compares the published version. Real complexification gives even quaternionic multiplicity. The entire monomial Hecke witness has negative root number. An isolated realization over ℚ and conjectural complex or quaternionic coefficient theories are outside the obstruction.','whole_source_obstruction_reconstructed','PAPER-GEO65-001')
c('OBS-SUZUKI-COMPENSATED-DRIFT-SIGN','drift','On page 6 of arXiv:2209.12832v2, the term +iCt outside the integral requires C = −B − Σ m/[γ(1 + γ²)]. The displayed coefficient has the opposite sign. The exact S♯ example F = 1 + 2i·4^(−s) gives −8 log 2/17 for the printed C and +8 log 2/17 for the required C.','Source equations (1.1) and (2.5)–(2.6), signed atoms −γ, and truncation x/(1 + x²) are fixed. The change is a deterministic translation. The Gaussian and jump measures, screw kernel, and real-part criterion are unchanged. Journal wording is unverified.','verified_versioned_auxiliary_representation_error','PAPER-POS64-OPPROB-018')
c('THM-SCALAR-PRIME-SUBPOWER-POLYNOMIAL','bands','Under RH, every subpower cutoff P(Y) → ∞ with log P = o(log Y) gives all fixed Gaussian moments of standardized W_P. At P = Y^θ with 0 < θ < 1/2, weak Gaussian convergence holds, and moments through 2k converge when kθ < 1/2.','Uses natural cosine coefficients 1/√p, exact H_P and V_P centering and variance, and the symmetric strict tail. The bounded-coefficient aggregate polynomial theorem precedes main-term expansion. The proof uses near-power truncation and an upper-band L^p bound. The endpoint θ = 1/2 and all moments at fixed θ remain outside the result.','conditional_extended_scalar_cutoff_limit')
c('THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-COVARIANCE','bands','Under RH, for 0 < a < b < 1/4, let Δ_j = b^j − a^j. The cosine band mean tends to log(b/a) − 4Δ₁ + 2Δ₃/3 and its variance tends to (1/2) log(b/a) − 4Δ₁² + 4Δ₁Δ₃ − 4Δ₃²/9. The sine mean is zero and its variance tends to (1/2) log(b/a) − (3/2)Δ₂². The mixed covariance is zero.','Fixed band Y^a < p ≤ Y^b, coefficients 1/√p, and the symmetric strict tail. Ratio and product kernels differ by 12x²y². The proof uses the exact diagonal and aggregate D² support with 2b < 1/2. Covariance test functions retain the finite-rank correction and positive lower bound.','conditional_first_second_moment_theorem')
c('THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-NONGAUSSIAN','bands','Under RH, for 0 < a < b < 1/6, the centered cosine band third moment tends to −8Δ₁³ + 24Δ₁²Δ₃ − 8Δ₁Δ₃² + 16Δ₃³/27 < 0. For [a,b] = [1/20, 1/10], the value is −818904257/864000000000. No centered Gaussian weak subsequence is possible.','Aggregate D³ support requires 3b < 1/2. The repeated-prime term (3/2)H times the mean cancels the corresponding second-moment diagonal. Uniform fourth moments from |Re D|⁴ ≤ |D²|² give uniform integrability of the cubes. The full limiting band law remains unproved.','conditional_non_gaussian_obstruction')
c('THM-ROOTED-CUE-PRIME-BAND-MOMENT-MATCH','bands','Globally derivative-square tilted rooted CUE has the same limiting cosine and sine means and covariance as the arithmetic band under RH, and the same centered cosine third moment for b < 1/6. Its projection is onto polynomials of degrees 0 through N with the rank-two span of constant and linear coefficient vectors removed.','Uses the HKO joint Haar matrix and root-label tilt, includes the selected root, and takes the negative Fourier band observable with weights 1/k. The correspondence is k/N ↔ log p/log Y. The random matrix statements are unconditional and the arithmetic comparison assumes RH. The match covers the band means, covariance, and cosine cubic. A full joint third-moment tensor and law transfer remain outside its scope.','exact_cross_framework_moment_match')
c('THM-SHARP-AGGREGATE-CONTINUOUS-J','bands','The sharp shifted continuous moment with a fixed polynomial has uniform error O_ε(T^ε[y√T + √y T^(3/4)]) for bounded coefficient families with y ≤ T^δ and fixed δ < 1/2. It holds for |α|, |β| ≤ c/log T with fixed small c, includes the weights 1 and log(t/(2π)), and treats the χ′/χ correction separately. It is unconditional.','The direct product approximate functional equation uses aggregated integer frequency gaps, a Mellin diagonal shift of −1/4, sharp endpoints, low heights, and holomorphic extension across coinciding shifts. The proof avoids applying Pratt–Robles smoothing outside its stated range.','independent_sharp_interface_reconstruction')
write('theorems/director_round11_claims.jsonl',C)
edges=[]
for a,b,k in [('THM-PRIME-BROWNIAN-PROCESS','THM-JOINT-PRIME-GAUSSIAN-ARRAY','joint'),('THM-JOINT-PRIME-GAUSSIAN-ARRAY','THM-EFFECTIVE-SCALAR-PRIME-CLT','joint'),('THM-FINITE-VARIANCE-PRIME-ANNULI','THM-JOINT-PRIME-GAUSSIAN-ARRAY','joint'),('THM-INTEGER-TOEPLITZ-PURITY','THM-FINITE-FROBENIUS-TRACE-CRITERION','matrix'),('CERT-GLOBAL-HARDY-C2','THM-WEIGHTED-VECTOR-ROLLE-TAIL','global'),('CERT-GLOBAL-HARDY-C2','CERT-Q2-SERIES-10000','global'),('THM-SCALAR-PRIME-SUBPOWER-POLYNOMIAL','THM-SHARP-AGGREGATE-CONTINUOUS-J','bands'),('THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-NONGAUSSIAN','THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-COVARIANCE','bands'),('THM-ROOTED-CUE-PRIME-BAND-MOMENT-MATCH','THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-NONGAUSSIAN','bands'),('THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-COVARIANCE','THM-SHARP-AGGREGATE-CONTINUOUS-J','bands')]:
 edges.append(dict(**{'from':a,'to':b},relation=('compares_to_classical_joint_trace_criterion' if k=='matrix' else 'uses_with_exact_recorded_scope'),evidence=N[k],locator=N[k],status='adjudicated_scoped'))
for ident in ['THM-SCALAR-PRIME-SUBPOWER-POLYNOMIAL','THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-COVARIANCE','THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-NONGAUSSIAN']:
 edges.append(dict(**{'from':ident,'to':'THM-HLZ-JOURNAL5-REAL-COEFFICIENTS'},relation='uses_published_primary_theorem_with_scoped_reconstruction',evidence=N['bands'],locator=N['bands'],status='adjudicated_scoped'))
write('theorems/director_round11_proof_edges.jsonl',edges)
spec=[('JOINT','joint',['uniform65_joint_exceptional_prime_clt.md','analytic67_joint_process_skeptic.md']),('PROCESS','joint',['uniform67_brownian_prime_phase_process.md','analytic67_joint_process_skeptic.md']),('MATRIX','matrix',['uniform69_integer_toeplitz_purity.md','geometry69_integer_toeplitz_skeptic.md']),('GLOBAL','global',['prime69_parameterized_hardy_tail.md','weighted69_hardy_parameter_review.md']),('DENINGER','deninger',['geometry68_deninger_whole_advocate.md','analytic68_deninger_whole_skeptic.md']),('DRIFT','drift',['uniform66_suzuki_compensated_drift.md','geometry66_suzuki_compensated_drift.md']),('CUTOFF','bands',['prime70_hlz_cutoff_extension.md','weighted70_hlz_cutoff_review.md']),('BAND2','bands',['prime71_hlz_band_covariance.md','weighted71_hlz_band_second_moment.md','geometry71_hlz_band_independent.md']),('BAND3','bands',['prime72_hlz_band_third_cumulant.md','weighted73_rooted_cue_band_match.md','analytic76_hlz_third_skeptic.md']),('SHARPJ','bands',['prime75_hlz_sharp_aggregate_review.md','weighted75_sharp_aggregate_review.md'])]
upsert('audits/reviewed_claim_groups.jsonl',[dict(id='REVIEW-GROUP-R11-'+i,title=i+' scoped source reconstruction',status='adjudicated_scoped',director_adjudication=N[k],independent_reviews=[A+x for x in rev]) for i,k,rev in spec])
promotion=dict(id='PAPER-GEO65-001',level=3,version='arXiv:2204.02714v2, author manuscript',arxiv_version='2204.02714v2',source_sha256='abef52f91f14b13f53602c5af2add8e657caffbcee984b288d3eaf8adca50e37',evidence=N['deninger'],independent_reviews=[A+'geometry68_deninger_whole_advocate.md',A+'analytic68_deninger_whole_skeptic.md'],whole_work_coverage_checklist=['All 8 pages and 17 references, comparison with the 9-page publisher version, and v1 history','Finite-field quaternion obstruction and conditional coefficient categories','All axioms 2.1–2.12, generalized eigenspaces, cup products, and positivity','Exact central multiplicity parity via two original Q₈ root-number routes','Nonzero hypothesis on Morin’s class map and counterexample to a blanket reading for isolated ℚ','Conjectural 2.14–2.15, foliations, half Tate twists, and boundaries of height results'],external_inputs='Uses the supersingular endomorphism theorem, standard motivic conjectures as conditional inputs, and the named Artin induction, Hecke, and original root-number criteria. The audit covers these inputs in their stated use.')
upsert('quality/whole_work_audit_promotions.jsonl',[promotion])
write('quality/zz_round11_source_scope_updates.jsonl',[dict(id=promotion['id'],evidence=N['deninger'],fields=dict(audit_level=3,whole_work_read=True,version=promotion['version'],source_sha256=promotion['source_sha256'],read_scope='The advocate, skeptic, and director independently read and reconstructed the complete eight-page arXiv v2. Includes two routes to the original root-number inputs, full journal comparison, and verification of the quantifiers in context.'))])
findings=[dict(id='FIND-SUZUKI-COMPENSATED-DRIFT-SIGN',classification='Verified mathematical error',title='Opposite compensated drift in pinned extended Selberg screw representation',sources=['PAPER-POS64-OPPROB-018','OBS-SUZUKI-COMPENSATED-DRIFT-SIGN'],scope='Limited to the printed coefficient of +iCt outside the integral in arXiv:2209.12832v2, page 6, §5.1. The kernel, real-part criterion, and infinite divisibility survive translation. Journal wording is unverified.',evidence=N['drift'],director_adjudication=N['drift'],verified_author_error=True,status='adjudicated_exact_versioned_auxiliary_representation_error',independent_reviews=[A+'uniform66_suzuki_compensated_drift.md',A+'geometry66_suzuki_compensated_drift.md'],explicit_witness='F = 1 + 2i·4^(−s) satisfies S♯, with GRH following by absolute values. Here B = −log 2 and A = 9 log 2/17. The printed C is −8 log 2/17 and the required C is +8 log 2/17.',date='2026-11-18'),dict(id='FIND-DENINGER-ISOLATED-FIELD-SCOPE',classification='Correct argument, but commonly misinterpreted',title='Real-descent obstruction needs an obstructed Artin sector or a universal family',sources=['PAPER-GEO65-001','THM-DENINGER-REAL-DESCENT-OBSTRUCTION'],scope='Theorem 2.13 is read in its global functorial context. Its obstruction does not extend to a blanket claim about an isolated operator over ℚ. The positive pairing remains conjectural.',evidence=N['deninger'],director_adjudication=N['deninger'],verified_author_error=False,status='adjudicated_scope_qualification',independent_reviews=promotion['independent_reviews'],date='2026-11-18')]
write('audits/director_round11_findings.jsonl',findings)
connections=[]
def cn(i,k,sources,statement,hyp,proved,open_,next_,risk,tests,significance):
 connections.append(dict(id=i,sources=sources,statement=statement,hypotheses=hyp,already_proved=proved,conjectural=open_,next_step=next_,counterexamples=risk,tests=tests,significance=significance,difficulty='See the proof and next step. Priority remains unresolved or the classical antecedent is credited.',status='adjudicated_scoped',evidence=N[k]))
cn('CONN-AGGREGATE-CUTOFF-EXTENSION','bands',['THM-SCALAR-PRIME-SUBPOWER-POLYNOMIAL','THM-SHARP-AGGREGATE-CONTINUOUS-J'],'Use the full shifted quadratic form before expansion to avoid exponential loss from summing individual character errors.','The zero law assumes RH. Uses bounded Dirichlet coefficients, padded divisor-closed families, and declared length below √T.','All fixed moments for subpower cutoffs and the weak scalar CLT at polynomial cutoffs.','All moments at fixed θ and general unbounded joint arrays remain unestablished.','Find a uniform higher-order main-term and error estimate or a fixed-band characteristic-function estimate.','An arbitrary fixed logarithmic saving cannot absorb exp(L^a) words. The polynomial local factor F differs from 1.','Independent reconstructions of aggregate padding, the sharp approximate functional equation, and strict Stieltjes integration.','Extends the earlier logarithmic cutoffs.')
cn('CONN-ROOTED-CUE-NONGAUSSIAN-BANDS','bands',['THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-COVARIANCE','THM-POLYNOMIAL-PRIME-BAND-NONGAUSSIAN','THM-ROOTED-CUE-PRIME-BAND-MOMENT-MATCH'],'The derivative-rooted CUE rank-two projection and exact HLZ local kernels give the same band means, covariance, and centered cosine third moment.','The covariance range is 0 < a < b < 1/4 and the cubic requires b < 1/6. Uses the symmetric derivative-weighted tail under RH and the global joint Haar matrix and root-label tilt.','Explicit means, rank-two and rank-one covariance corrections, a negative cubic, and exclusion of Gaussian weak subsequences.','The full band law and matching higher moments remain open.','Characterize the candidate DPP band law and the exact arithmetic estimate needed to transfer it.','Normalizing root-label sampling within each matrix gives a different measure. Matching these moments does not identify the law.','Three independent HLZ extractions, exact CUE projection traces, and uniform fourth moments.','Connects the arithmetic and random matrix calculations through explicit moments.')
cn('CONN-LOCAL-MASS-PROCESS-TIGHTNESS','joint',['THM-JOINT-PRIME-GAUSSIAN-ARRAY','THM-PRIME-BROWNIAN-PROCESS'],'Local reciprocal-mass fourth moments turn finite-dimensional arithmetic phase comparison into Brownian path convergence.','Assumes RH and uses the fixed Brownian logarithmic clock and symmetric strict tail.','An all-time interpolated increment bound, an effective modulus, and the J₁ limit.','Larger-cutoff processes and numerical rates at finite Y require separate research.','Extend the local mass bound to larger cutoffs without introducing an interval-independent error.','Finite-dimensional convergence alone does not give tightness. The wrong log-power clock gives perfectly correlated limits.','Independent three-piece interpolation and dyadic chaining.','The tightness argument specifies the clock and sampling measure.')
cn('CONN-INTEGER-TRACE-CLASSICAL-TOEPLITZ','matrix',['THM-INTEGER-TOEPLITZ-PURITY','THM-INTEGRAL-TRACE-FINITE-CUTOFF'],'Classical power-sum Toeplitz inertia becomes an exact low-index integer purity certificate by arithmetic congruence.','One fixed monic integral q-reciprocal spectrum with positive multiplicities.','A positive semidefiniteness criterion and inertia from traces through d − 1, with a polynomial-bit algorithm.','An infinite trace realization of the classical zeta function remains open.','Test candidate finite Frobenius models with K, then prove compatible trace and positivity limits.','Individual two-term tests and leading minors alone fail. The ordinary Schur–Cohn form vanishes.','Independent Vandermonde congruences and exact singular, repeated-root, and nonsquare cases.','Makes the existing criterion computationally usable and credits its antecedent.')
cn('CONN-DENINGER-REAL-QUATERNIONIC-BOUNDARY','deninger',['THM-DENINGER-REAL-DESCENT-OBSTRUCTION'],'An Artin root-number parity supplies an exact obstruction to ordinary real functorial spectral descent.','Central Artin multiplicity compatibility and a field with a negative-sign quaternionic sector.','The multiplicity contradiction excludes a universal ordinary real theory.','Constructing positive complex or quaternionic cohomology or an isolated operator over ℚ remains open.','Specify the Galois-equivariant star and prove positivity on every spectral sector.','Even parity of the whole space or height positivity on a subsector is insufficient.','Independent original root-number witnesses and the antilinear map on the Hom space with square −1.','Identifies the hypotheses of a known structural obstruction.')
write('connections/director_round11_connections.jsonl',connections)
